bug_report:
flexible array initialization is allowed when initialized with `{}` with C23
Take:
```
struct f {
  int t;
  int tt[];
};

struct f b = {1, {}};
```

This is should be rejected with -pedantic-errors since initializing flexible array is an extension.  If we change `{}` to `{1}` then we reject it correct.
clang rejects it in both cases.

I think this is the same cause asPR 65673and might be solved by the same way as suggested byhttps://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=65673#c3.

Especially since the comment is not correct for C23:
      /* Silently discard empty initializations.  The parser will
         already have pedwarned for empty brackets.  */
